{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.baselineX_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.baselineX_pos","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L231-L244","doc":"The baseline is **positive** for every `q > 1` — the neutron is the heavier\nnucleon, in the model's own sign convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.framing_weight_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.framing_weight_unique","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L212-L229","doc":"**`w = 1` is the only integer framing weight that works.**  If `q^w·X` obeys\nthe bar-odd law then `q ^ (2 - w) = q ^ w`, and for `1 < q` the power function is\ninjective, so `w = 1`.\n\nStated on the exponent arithmetic rather than on `X` itself, because that is\nwhere the content is: the bar ratio of `X` is the monomial `-q²`, so the\ncondition `q^{-w}·(-q²) = -q^w` reduces to `2 - w = w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.q_mul_baselineX_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.q_mul_baselineX_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L201-L206","doc":"**One unit of framing makes it bar-odd.**  `q·X_baseline` satisfies the\nbar-odd law exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.baselineX_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.baselineX_bar","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L193-L199","doc":"**The baseline is neither bar-even nor bar-odd**: the bar involution\nmultiplies it by `-q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.baselineX_eq_prefactor_mul_symValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.baselineX_eq_prefactor_mul_symValue","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L186-L191","doc":"The displayed baseline is the `k = 2` form `ℏ_q²(q² - q⁻²)/3` — the identity\nthat locates the prefactor as `ℏ_q²/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.hbarSq_eq_scaled_barNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.hbarSq_eq_scaled_barNorm","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L173-L180","doc":"**`ℏ_q²` is the instance at `f = ℏ`.**  `q⁻¹ · barNorm hbarOf q = ℏ_q²`,\nexactly — so the corpus's prefactor is `q⁻¹` times the bar-norm of `ℏ_q`, and its\nparity is then a corollary of `barNorm_scaled_parity` rather than a coincidence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.barNorm_scaled_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.barNorm_scaled_parity","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L165-L171","doc":"**`q⁻¹` times a bar-norm satisfies the parity constraint automatically.**\nThis is the structural content: the condition `C(q⁻¹) = q²·C(q)` that §1 measured\nof `ℏ_q²` is not special to `ℏ_q` — it holds of `q⁻¹ · barNorm f` for every `f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.barNorm_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.barNorm_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L158-L163","doc":"**A bar-norm is bar-even, for every `f`** — no hypothesis on `f` at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.barNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.barNorm","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L155-L156","doc":"The bar-norm of `f` at `q`: `-(f q · f q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.q_mul_hbarSq_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.q_mul_hbarSq_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L122-L127","doc":"`q·ℏ_q²` is **bar-even**, which is the same fact stated on the prefactor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.q_mul_hbarSq_eq_barNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.q_mul_hbarSq_eq_barNorm","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L113-L120","doc":"**The prefactor is `q⁻¹` times the bar-norm of `ℏ_q`.**\n`q·ℏ_q² = (q-1)²/q = -ℏ_q·ℏ_{q⁻¹}`, exactly.  This is the sharpest positive\nstatement in the file, and it is an identity, not a derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.pi_partner_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.pi_partner_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L108-L111","doc":"`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` is **bar-even** — the `cosh`-like partner shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.symValue_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.symValue_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L101-L106","doc":"`q² - q⁻²` is **bar-odd**: the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` negates it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.baselineX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.baselineX","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L98-L99","doc":"The block's displayed baseline `X_baseline(q) = (q-1)²(1 - q⁻⁴)/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.symValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.symValue","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L95-L96","doc":"The `k = 2` crossing-reversal value `q² - q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.hbarOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitBarParity.hbarOf","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitBarParity.lean#L92-L93","doc":"`ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}